    "statement": "Switching off the in-state non-brand search campaigns in Metro 2 and Metro 4 for 8 weeks lowers intake there, against the control-based counterfactual, by at least 50% of the conversions Google credits to those metros.",
    "success_criterion": "The 95% interval's lower end is above 50% incrementality (the decision rule below).",
    "validity_checks": [
      "Tracking check passed before launch: intake records log each lead's location the same way in every holdout and control metro.",
      "Back-test passes at 8 weeks (it does on the pre-period).",
      "Holdout spend near zero from the first day.",
      "No edits to scope campaigns during the test, and every outside event logged."
    ]
  },
